<%# FUIME: the layout for a hosted payment page.

    Its own layout rather than `application` or `bare`, for one reason: this page
    is reached from somewhere else. A buyer clicks a link on a teenager's Replit
    site, an Instagram bio or a DM, and lands here cold — with no idea what Fuime
    is and no reason to trust it yet.

    So there is no app chrome, no nav, no sidebar and nothing to click away to
    except the business's own storefront. What a stranger needs is: what am I
    buying, from whom, how much, and who is taking my card. Everything else is
    noise on the one screen where noise costs a teenager a sale.

    `bare: true` on the head partial for the same reason the login layout uses
    it — no command bar, no signed-in machinery, on a page nobody is signed in
    to. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <%= render "layouts/head", bare: true %>
  </head>
  <body class="fuime-payment-page">
    <main class="mx-auto px-4 py-10" style="max-width: 30rem;">
      <%= yield %>
    </main>

    <%# The standing disclosure. It is not decoration and it is not optional:
        L5 requires it wherever Fuime describes what it is, and this page is
        seen by more strangers than any authenticated page will ever be. %>
    <footer class="mx-auto px-4 pb-10 text-center" style="max-width: 30rem;">
      <p class="text-sm muted mb-1">
        Payments by <strong>Fuime</strong>, the financial platform for young
        founders. Card details are handled by Stripe — Fuime never sees them.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm muted mt-0 mb-0">
        Fuime is a financial technology company, not a bank. Fuime does not take
        deposits and does not offer FDIC-insured products.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
